  "body": "## What\n\nBoth `mcc-claude` and `fcc-claude` (they resolve to the same entry point, `cli.launchers.claude:launch`) now set `ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS=true` on the launched Claude Code session.\n\nWeb server tools need the proxy-side execution path, so sessions launched through the proxy should always have them available. The variable is forced in `build_minimal_claude_proxy_env` — the env policy used **only** by this launcher — so the `-old` / legacy launcher (`launch_legacy`, full-env builder) is untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `build_minimal_claude_proxy_env` now emits `ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS=true`; the two env-shape tests updated and assert it.\n- `launch([\"--model\", \"sonnet\"])` child env includes `ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS=true`; the `changed`-set assertion updated to include it.\n- 13 claude launcher/env tests pass; full `test_entrypoints.py` 84 pass.\n- 2 `test_web_server_tools.py` failures are pre-existing on unmodified `fork/main` (verified via baseline worktree), unrelated to this change.\n- ruff format/check and ty clean.\n\nVersion 5.2.2 → 5.3.0 (launcher behavior addition).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
